<pdd-reason>Switching between plans is the PRD's headline verb and needs a server-side pointer the CLI and GUI both read.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "api",
  "api": {
    "endpoints": [
      {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/plans/active",
        "auth": "none",
        "responseSchema": "PlanMeta + rev"
      },
      {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/api/plans/active",
        "auth": "none",
        "requestSchema": "{slug: string}",
        "responseSchema": "PlanMeta + rev",
        "errors": [
          "404 unknown slug",
          "409 while mix_state.running"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>
<pdd-dependency>brain/plan_store_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-dependency>brain/plan_context_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-dependency>brain/api_router_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/api/api_plans_active.py` as the GET returns the currently active plan payload. POST {slug} sets the pointer and returns the plan. REFUSES WITH 409 WHILE app.mix_state.running: switching the active plan under a live run is the same class of race as pulling a track out of a playing set. An unknown slug is a 404 and leaves the pointer unchanged. REACHABILITY: this route only resolves because api_router scores a literal segment above a <param> segment; registered naively it is swallowed by /api/plans/<slug>. The reserved-slug set in plan_types is the second, independent defense, since the router rule does not stop a plans/active/ directory from shadowing active.json on disk.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

GET returns the currently active plan payload. POST {slug} sets the pointer and returns the plan. REFUSES WITH 409 WHILE app.mix_state.running: switching the active plan under a live run is the same class of race as pulling a track out of a playing set. An unknown slug is a 404 and leaves the pointer unchanged. REACHABILITY: this route only resolves because api_router scores a literal segment above a <param> segment; registered naively it is swallowed by /api/plans/<slug>. The reserved-slug set in plan_types is the second, independent defense, since the router rule does not stop a plans/active/ directory from shadowing active.json on disk.

